rac{1}{2}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=\\frac{(-2)(-1)+(-2)(-1)}{4}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-3,-1)}=\\frac{(-2)(-3)+(-2)(-1)}{4}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/f5/f51fb78a12bc37626954936b6f001ff807b97c0c55279314ec60f61ecbfde501.png)" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670674 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670697 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670674 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670674 1071 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3x^{2}-(3)y?$" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670674 1072 #uuid "459e46c9-4184-5656-bb8b-3280b2551168" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670674 1074 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,0)$,$(-1,-1)$,$(-1,3)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,0)}=3(-2)^{2}-3(0)=12, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=3(-1)^{2}-3(-1)=6, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=3(-1)^{2}-3(3)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/b9/b91833eba8558d82b86f66bbc5889f2a6bb2187178170846c12238a3027cd2a0.png)" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670675 1068 #edb/ref 17592186670688 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670675 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670675 1071 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-1-(2)xy?$" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670675 1072 #uuid "4a81fec4-e469-52d1-b3ae-2d2d1e2bd280" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670675 1074 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(3,-2)$,$(2,-2)$,$(0,-2)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,-2)}=-1-2(3)(-2)=11, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=-1-2(2)(-2)=7, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,-2)}=-1-2(0)(-2)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/da/da38e55a37f775b3e531b61436ff070901cd88f7ce4a7c9229f096e87159c3c8.png)" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670676 1080 "images/7d/7d47d65a715204c6b220483ef4373d3f7cf066812f6265f34f8b90be599fd2b0.png" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670676 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670676 1083 #uuid "4e721f05-03da-5b8a-ad50-2d1b49465988" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670677 1080 "images/42/42df4bf8c25e644e5ddfc47623e2e7a391d897ed8ceeb72b429f0b29e5fca2f1.png" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670677 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670677 1083 #uuid "52188b34-0248-5085-a960-b7d7eec72d11" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670678 1080 "images/cf/cf3ae6090229f1b66486c3606840c74a07be0a37559e06bd3429dec9c458a070.png" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670678 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670678 1083 #uuid "547596f5-e0bd-55eb-967b-d130fc7d15d8" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670679 1080 "images/f9/f99bc2a1d6becc2fe69d65bc6d9b83412e4f6f225059ba65953fbf5c84cca41d.png" 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670679 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 13194139538541 17592186045443 true] [17592186670679 1083 #uuid "56d25aaf-37ff-585d-9a1c-dcf9044262ec" 13194139538541 17592